{"author":{"id":"d4d77c46d796577aec35d160aa1e09aa095720b03e93f3ca34ad3c079140e2fb"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794739807,"nonce":"sIenY3dArzmXtk+TSJNJ90OSjmM=","message":"A second reason to change the names: MoltenVK translates SPIR-V to MSL with SPIRV-Cross, and a render pipeline whose SPIR-V entry points are named vertex and fragment produces MSL that does not compile (MoltenVK 1.2.11, from hxn-gpu-vulkan's check). If hxnsl named its WGSL entry points so that no target reserves them (vertex_main, fragment_main, compute_main, say), every language would carry the same names, Naga would rename nothing, and this issue and the MoltenVK failure would both go. It changes ENTRY_POINTS' names, which is breaking for 0.1.0.","files":null}]}